se the witnesses exclude, deny or establish something must quote the words that state it; where the quoted words, read in their own context and with the other verses the judge quotes, do not state it, the ground is the judge's own [L4] inference, and it counts only when the judge exhibits two lower layers ([L1]-[L3]) for it, as submitted evidence must; otherwise it is no ground for BROKEN, and the link is graded under the remaining rules. Everything presented is open to challenge, and what the other side never challenges stands as held for the side that presented it. VERSE CITATION (binding, operator ruling 3): cite every verse by book, chapter and verse (for example Matthew 1:25) and quote its words exactly as the KJV gives them; a quotation may be part of a verse. A verse alluded to, paraphrased or misquoted, or named without its book, chapter and verse, is not counted as evidence or as an answer, and the system checks every quotation against the KJV text. After the link rounds you have a CLOSE ROUND: your final words on your own position, in which you may not press any new witness or premise.";
