const PROVE="\n\nPROVE YOUR POSITIONS. Prove every position with the layers. A statement of your position is not proof of it.\nEvery claim that a verse means, shows, requires or excludes something carries its layers: the verse quoted with its reference [L1], and at least one more layer, either a Hebrew or Greek word with its meaning [L2] or another verse quoted with its reference [L3]. A claim given without its layers carries no weight with the judges. A correction is answered on the chain, with book, chapter and verse; no stock phrase stands in for an answer, and a sentence that only defers a point to review is a defect, not an answer. A link is graded by what its scripture carries, whatever label its own side gives it: a link that assumes as given a fact about a person, house, time or act that no quoted row gives is unexhibited, and a narrowed link whose kept words still assert what its side gave up counts as conceded; what a link infers from its rows is its [L4], footed on two lower layers, and need not be stated by any row (DG-61).";
const __BARRED="\n\nBARRED MOVES. Four moves are barred to both sides. Each example is from one of our runs.\n(a) An answer from silence: answering a press from what a verse does not name, state or say. Run 33107 [CR3]: \"They do not name the parent.\" Run 33149 [CR4]: \"It does not say through whom.\"\n(b) A requirement the verse never sets: asking a verse to state what it never sets out to state, and counting its silence against the other side. Run 33160 [CR4]: Mary asks how, and the answer does not say \"when Joseph takes you.\"\n(c) Answering the verse but not the press's MEANS: naming or quoting the pressed verse without meeting the meaning the press claims for it. Run 33160 [DR3]: the press on Matthew 1:19 claimed it MEANS \"a husband who knew himself the father would have no cause to put her away\"; the answer gave the verse's words (\"being a just [man]... was minded to put her away privily\") and their Greek, and never met that meaning.\n(d) Granting a row and then acting as if it were not granted. Run 33107: [CR3] \"I grant that \"born of a woman\" is said of men with fathers.\" Then [CR4] rested the source on that same row: \"Galatians 4:4 puts the same woman as the source.\"\nAnswer every press positively: quote the words a verse does state ([L1], with its reference) and say what they carry. When a sentence of yours only denies a requirement the other side imposed, write directly under it: NOT A REQUIREMENT -- rebuts [<the other side's round>] \"<their words, 6 or more, word for word>\". The system finds (a) and (b) in code. A round that carries one is sent back to you once; a sentence that still carries one after that is VOID: the system strikes it from the round, the press it answered counts as unanswered, and the offense is named in the run report. Repeated offenses will result in disqualification.";
