K graded MISSES or FAILS, or CHANGE TO the IMPOSED line SET BY [L1] <reference> \"<the KJV words that set it>\". A KEEP does not cure this item.':'\\nTHE IMPOSED REQUIREMENT RULE (E-IMP, ENFORCED, pkgIMP; Commitment 14): the sentence above rests an answer on a verse not stating something (\"'+i.imp.phrase+'\"). That asks the verse to hold a requirement; it is an answer only when a row of scripture sets that requirement. CHANGE TO one line: IMPOSED: ['+i.imp.round+'] \"<the sentence, quoted>\" -- asks <verse> to <what it is asked to state> -- NO ROW SETS IT, or SET BY [L1] <reference> \"<the KJV words that set it>\". The KJV words are counted. A KEEP does not cure this item.');","const __mnpR=i=>!i.mnp?'':'\\nTHE MEANS RULE (E-MNP, ENFORCED, pkgMNP): your ANSWER CHECK says this press has no MEANS. The press ledger reads its MEANS in ['+(i.mnp.round[0]==='C'?'DR2':'CR3')+'] (premise '+i.mnp.premise+'): \"'+i.mnp.ledger_means+'\". The ledger marks the press '+i.mnp.ledger_cls+'. CHANGE TO the ANSWER CHECK line for '+i.mnp.ref+' with that MEANS quoted (at least 6 words in a row of it, or all of it if shorter) and the answer graded MEETS or MISSES'+(i.mnp.ledger_cls==='UNPROVEN'?' (or UNPROVEN, as the ledger marks it)':'')+'. A KEEP does not cure this item.';","const __pabR=i=>!i.pab?'':'\\nTHE PRESS ABSENCE RULE (E-PAB, ENFORCED, pkgPAB; Commitment 3 with Commitment 5): your line charges the press '+i.pab.ref+' ['+i.pab.round+'] as unanswered. A press proves only what its quoted words show; its MEANS reads \"'+i.pab.means+'\", and the part \"'+i.pab.absence.join('; ')+'\" is an absence (what a verse does not state), which presses nothing. '+(i.pab.positive?'To keep the line, KEEP it with a sentence that quotes the positive part of that MEANS the charge rests on (at least 6 words in a row of \"'+i.pab.positive+'\", or all of it if shorter) and says why that part was left unanswered. ':'This MEANS has no positive part, so a KEEP cannot cure it. ')+'Otherwise CHANGE TO the