rary, with no round named that answered the witness): A link marked STANDS, or a collision graded UNDERDETERMINED, against a pressed witness the other side exhibited (a verse a listed premise carries under PRESSED WITH:, md_notes_rulings 392) names in the same line the round that answered that witness. A pressed witness (a verse a listed premise carries under PRESSED WITH:, md_notes_rulings 392) left unanswered is a BROKEN ground; a verse under no PRESSED WITH: line, left unanswered, is no BROKEN ground. That a single verse does not state a link or its contrary is never a ground for STANDS or UNDERDETERMINED, for either side. Cure it with one RESTATED line for that link (D<n> vs C<m>, or D<n> for a STANDS line), regraded: it names the round that answered the witness ([CR2], [CR3] or [CR4] for a defender link, [DR1], [DR2] or [DR3] for a challenger link), or it grades the line LINK BROKEN, with exactly one CORRECTED RESULT. \""," +\"K-C (a line that sets aside a chained premise, or a side's rows read together, on the ground that no one verse in them states the link or its contrary in its own words; the item quotes the line and the chain it set aside): that is never a ground, for the rows are weighed together, line upon line. If the ground you drop was the only ground your RESULT gave for its winner, your cure also writes a CORRECTED RESULT that names a new ground from the exhibited chains, or reads UNDERDETERMINED (run 32677: a restated RESULT kept its winner with no ground). \""," +\"Cure it with one RESTATED line for the item that grades it on the chain as a whole: it drops that ground and names the footing of the chain it weighed, exhibiting at least two kinds of layer, each tagged as the layer rule reads: [L1] with the KJV words quoted; [L2] with the Hebrew or Greek word in its own script, with its transliteration marks, with its Strong's number, or in plain letters with its English meaning beside it (\\\"[L2] genomenou (made)\\\", \\\"[L2] sperma, seed\\\"), the